INT. FERRY TERMINAL LOST PROPERTY OFFICE - NIGHT

Shelves of umbrellas. A cage of single gloves. Fluorescent hum.

DET. ROSALIND IKEDA leans on the counter. AUGUSTIN BEAUMONT, the clerk, hides behind a ledger. LUCINDA MORROW sits on a bench with a violin case on her knees. KWAME ASANTE paces. OFFICER PERRY blocks the door.

IKEDA
Describe the case again.

LUCINDA
Black. Brass clasps. A sticker of a lighthouse on the lid.

AUGUSTIN
We have forty-one black cases. Nine with brass.

KWAME
That one's hers. That one in her lap.

LUCINDA
This one is mine. Yours is somewhere else.

IKEDA
Open it.

LUCINDA
It's a violin.

IKEDA
Then it won't mind.

AUGUSTIN
Detective, there are procedures.

IKEDA
Mr. Beaumont, you logged this case at nine-ten. Two hours before the ferry docked.

AUGUSTIN
I may have mistaken the time.

KWAME
He mistakes everything.

LUCINDA
Kwame, sit down.

KWAME
I've been sitting since Tuesday.

IKEDA
Officer Perry, the door.

PERRY
Locked, ma'am.

IKEDA
Miss Morrow. The clasps.

LUCINDA
No.

IKEDA
Then I'll count to three.

AUGUSTIN
Please don't.

KWAME
One.
